# Every endpoint as a runnable request.
# Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension. The JetBrains HTTP Client reads the same file, but write
# {{order.response.body.data.id}} there instead of {{order.response.body.$.data.id}}.
# Start the API first: docker compose up -d --build

@host = http://localhost:8080
@reseller = pxc_local_reseller_1_key
@admin = pxc_local_admin_key

### Health (no key)
GET {{host}}/health

### List products
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?category=synth&per_page=5
X-API-Key: {{reseller}}

### One product, with available_keys
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/12
X-API-Key: {{reseller}}

### Place an order (the same idempotency_key returns the same order)
# @name order
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
X-API-Key: {{reseller}}

{"product_id": 12, "quantity": 2, "idempotency_key": "http-file-1"}

### Read the order (uses the id from the request above)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{order.response.body.$.data.id}}
X-API-Key: {{reseller}}

### Reseller 1's order history
GET {{host}}/api/v1/resellers/1/orders?per_page=5
X-API-Key: {{reseller}}

### Trace the order (admin)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/support/orders/{{order.response.body.$.data.id}}/trace
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

### Cancel the order (admin): its keys are revoked, never resold
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{order.response.body.$.data.id}}/cancel
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

### Create a reseller (admin): the api_key in the response is shown once
POST {{host}}/api/v1/resellers
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

{"name": "My Shop", "country": "CA"}

### Import a catalog (admin): bad rows are rejected with reasons, good rows import
POST {{host}}/api/v1/catalog/import
X-API-Key: {{admin}}

{
  "vendor": "Example Audio",
  "products": [
    {"sku": "EX-SYNTH-001", "name": "Example Synth", "category": "synth", "price_cents": 4999,
     "keys": ["EX-SYN-0001", "EX-SYN-0002", "EX-SYN-0003"]},
    {"sku": "EX-BAD-001", "name": "Bad price", "category": "effect", "price_cents": 0, "keys": []}
  ]
}

### Error example: out of stock (product 8 has only 3 keys) -> 409 INSUFFICIENT_STOCK
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
X-API-Key: {{reseller}}

{"product_id": 8, "quantity": 5}

### Error example: no key -> 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products
